The @latest sentinel is resolved before the write: the marker lands the id of the plugin's
newest shipped migration, which moves whenever a migration ships — hence the wildcard. The
follow-up config-get pins it down as a real integer id: a marker still carrying the literal
sentinel fails to load and would exit non-zero there.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
# booping project marker
project_name: "demo"  # quoted on purpose
vault_path: ./vault
-- cmd --
booping marker-set latest_migration=@latest
booping config-get home_dir
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
~/Claude/
-- stderr --
marker: latest_migration=[..]
-- expected/cwd/.booping --
# booping project marker
project_name: "demo"  # quoted on purpose
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: [..]
